{"schemaVersion":1,"storyId":"rhyme-where-does-the-rain-go","version":1,"title":"Where Does the Rain Come From? (a rain song)","ageTiers":["5-6","7-8"],"language":"en","narrationLocale":"en-GH","pages":[{"n":1,"text":"The warm sun shines on the water below,\nIt lifts up tiny drops, high and slow.","sentences":["The warm sun shines on the water below,\nIt lifts up tiny drops, high and slow."],"alt":"Sunlight on a river with mist rising.","image":{"hash":"sha256:ebedba72e46e66681d86ee9d13a0f4082bed357d6fcce718037a7864d93c9bcf","width":960,"height":717},"audio":{"hash":"sha256:feb02fa81e1421ff44a28f1f77eeb13395aa8c162f6716903eb05c4074c7db82","durationMs":11840,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,11840]],"words":[[0,534],[534,1246],[1246,1780],[1780,2849],[2849,3205],[3205,3739],[3739,4629],[4629,5786],[5786,6143],[6143,7033],[7033,7389],[7389,8101],[8101,9258],[9258,9971],[9971,10505],[10505,11840]]}}},{"n":2,"text":"Up in the sky the drops cool and meet,\nThey make a cloud, soft and neat.","sentences":["Up in the sky the drops cool and meet,\nThey make a cloud, soft and neat."],"alt":"A small white cloud forming over a river.","image":{"hash":"sha256:9e82440113d1a1036183515e5aaf3fec08a7cdcbb6f60400e54e471ccf1e9ae9","width":960,"height":717},"audio":{"hash":"sha256:3503dcd5332151b24dc1aee4ab73789a105e9d34d90c08b91bf84a62e24a1d95","durationMs":10480,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,10480]],"words":[[0,346],[346,693],[693,1213],[1213,1732],[1732,2252],[2252,3118],[3118,3811],[3811,4331],[4331,5283],[5283,5976],[5976,6669],[6669,6842],[6842,7968],[7968,8661],[8661,9181],[9181,10480]]}}},{"n":3,"text":"The cloud grows heavy and cannot hold,\nSo down comes the rain, silver and cold.","sentences":["The cloud grows heavy and cannot hold,\nSo down comes the rain, silver and cold."],"alt":"A dark cloud with rain falling.","image":{"hash":"sha256:186d3f67929ef25b966101cc9c0446d01e443d3f2fa9c2df5a9b69a32ec2c989","width":960,"height":717},"audio":{"hash":"sha256:b739be84df7f452cc258f743a18bdab0604269d8a259a8514659f5244ec3665b","durationMs":11280,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,11280]],"words":[[0,494],[494,1317],[1317,2141],[2141,2964],[2964,3458],[3458,4446],[4446,5352],[5352,5681],[5681,6340],[6340,7163],[7163,7657],[7657,8563],[8563,9551],[9551,10045],[10045,11280]]}}},{"n":4,"text":"Pitter, patter on the roof it goes,\nIt waters the farm where the maize grows.","sentences":["Pitter, patter on the roof it goes,\nIt waters the farm where the maize grows."],"alt":"Rain on a tin roof and on a field of young maize.","image":{"hash":"sha256:9122b4465d6f2908dcb76aa82a932ebf2666b627cd489f59bf383a48ac8a954c","width":960,"height":717},"audio":{"hash":"sha256:cbe9e3bab6301d678c4a70ce55d5bb633a392870db5d9ec67f411a1bf0a99b59","durationMs":10360,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,10360]],"words":[[0,1168],[1168,2103],[2103,2415],[2415,2882],[2882,3505],[3505,3817],[3817,4674],[4674,4985],[4985,5920],[5920,6387],[6387,7011],[7011,7789],[7789,8257],[8257,9036],[9036,10360]]}}},{"n":5,"text":"It runs to the river and on to the sea,\nThen up it goes again. Wait and see!","sentences":["It runs to the river and on to the sea,\nThen up it goes again.","Wait and see!"],"alt":"A stream flowing to a river and a sunny sky.","image":{"hash":"sha256:300715979a945c6010e5906e2b77a7eb717c3db44da6cee69bf4d432cd1eaf93","width":960,"height":717},"audio":{"hash":"sha256:3386351f89a2f2df65ca9b2919b30d31612bdd923cf0c70858cde1fb9888a411","durationMs":10880,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,8603],[8603,10880]],"words":[[0,337],[337,1012],[1012,1349],[1349,1856],[1856,2699],[2699,3205],[3205,3542],[3542,3880],[3880,4386],[4386,5145],[5145,5820],[5820,6157],[6157,6494],[6494,7169],[7169,8603],[8603,9278],[9278,9784],[9784,10880]]}}}],"activities":[{"id":"rn-c1","type":"comprehension","afterPage":1,"question":"What lifts the water up into the sky?","options":["The warm sun","The moon","A bird"],"correctIndex":0},{"id":"rn-ph","type":"phonics","afterPage":3,"targetSound":"old","prompt":"Which word rhymes with cold?","options":["hold","rain","cloud"],"correctIndexes":[0]},{"id":"rn-s1","type":"sequencing","prompt":"Put the water journey in order.","items":["The sun warms the river.","Drops rise and make a cloud.","Rain falls from the cloud.","Water runs back to the river."]},{"id":"rn-voc","type":"vocabulary","afterPage":2,"word":"cloud","definition":"A mass of tiny water drops floating in the sky.","distractors":["A hill of sand","A kind of rain boot"]},{"id":"rn-sel","type":"sel","afterPage":5,"prompt":"How do you feel when the rain comes?","feelingOptions":["Happy","Cool","Excited","Sleepy"]}],"glossary":[{"word":"cloud","definition":"Tiny drops of water floating together in the sky.","pages":[2,3]},{"word":"maize","definition":"A tall crop with yellow grains, also called corn.","pages":[4]},{"word":"river","definition":"A large stream of water flowing to the sea.","pages":[5]}],"assets":{"sha256:ebedba72e46e66681d86ee9d13a0f4082bed357d6fcce718037a7864d93c9bcf":{"path":"/story-spark-preview/candidates/rhyme-where-does-the-rain-go/page1-1.webp","bytes":73098,"type":"image/webp"},"sha256:feb02fa81e1421ff44a28f1f77eeb13395aa8c162f6716903eb05c4074c7db82":{"path":"/story-spark-preview/audio/feb02fa81e14.mp3","bytes":95468,"type":"audio/mpeg"},"sha256:9e82440113d1a1036183515e5aaf3fec08a7cdcbb6f60400e54e471ccf1e9ae9":{"path":"/story-spark-preview/candidates/rhyme-where-does-the-rain-go/page2-1.webp","bytes":53330,"type":"image/webp"},"sha256:3503dcd5332151b24dc1aee4ab73789a105e9d34d90c08b91bf84a62e24a1d95":{"path":"/story-spark-preview/audio/3503dcd53321.mp3","bytes":84524,"type":"audio/mpeg"},"sha256:186d3f67929ef25b966101cc9c0446d01e443d3f2fa9c2df5a9b69a32ec2c989":{"path":"/story-spark-preview/can